        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 67,
      "title": "Reverting an act that renamed another card",
      "reason": "Ruby builds the revert as an update of this card with the other card's revision as a subcard (revision.rb merge_revert_action!), stores both reverted rows, and then raises Card::Error \"stage finalize was skipped\" for this card: the request fails after writing the reverted content and the other card's old name with no action or change rows, leaving an act with no actions and four card_changes rows whose actions were never stored (outsideRows). The TypeScript engine refuses the same request before writing anything (revert-unsupported). Both report a failure; the stored difference is the history-less half-applied revert. Candidate for an upstream fix.",
